DESCRIPTION:*******************************************\nLesson 8 Writing:
  Maya Social Organization\n\n*******************************************\n
 \n[Uploaded Image] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/36994/files/135775
 14/download?download_frd=1&hidden=1)\n\n \n\n   Introduction\n---------
 ------\n\nThe Maya have left some of the best evidence regarding urban lif
 e in pre-colonial times. Large cities ruled by elites from royal lineages 
 were occupied by hundreds of thousands of people in southern Mexico and no
 rthern Central America. Key to understanding these royal lines of authorit
 y was an advanced writing system developed by the Maya that only recently 
 has been deciphered. Stone monuments and buildings were erected by rulers 
 to mark important dates and events.\n\n   Instructions\n---------------
 \n\nTo get a better understanding of these people\, watch the following fi
 lm\, Lost King of the Maya\, about the ancient Maya city of Copan found in
  modern-day Honduras. As you are watching\, identify at least three conclu
 sions that archaeologists have made regarding Maya social organization men
 tioned in the film. For each one\, do the following:\n\n* Identify the asp
 ect of Maya society discovered by archaeologists in the film (1-2 sentence
 s).\n\n* Describe the lines of evidence that allowed archaeologists to arr
 ive at these conclusions about social life among the Maya (1-2 sentences).
 \n\nNumber the conclusions 1 through 3 and include all the required inform
 ation (10 pts each). Here is an example of how this should look (this is s
 imply an example and not one you should use for your assignment):\n\n1. Ma
 ya kings used psychedelic drugs that took them on spiritual journeys to th
 e underworld\, which legitimized their power. Archaeologists identified wi
 ld tobacco and datura residue in pipes found in elite burials at the site.
  Depictions of possible drug-induced journeys were also found depicted in 
 painted scenes on pottery and temple walls.\n\n   Lost King of the Maya
 \n------------------------\n\nTranscript Forthcoming\n\n \n\nImage Credit
 s\n-------------\n\nMike Searcy\, Eagle's Watch 2\, Mike Searcy\, Used wit
 h Permission.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)\n\n 
