 — Neanderthal\n*************************************\n\n[] (https://byu.
 instructure.com/courses/36994/files/13577542/download?download_frd=1&hidde
 n=1)\n\n \n\n---------------\n   Instructions\n---------------\n\nWatch
  the [BBC - Horizon - 2005 - Neanderthal] (https://dai.ly/x2269y9) on the 
 DailyMotion. Then identify three methods used in the film by researchers t
 o explore Neanderthal biology.\n\nNumber them 1-3. For each method\, brief
 ly describe:\n\n* Conclusions derived from the study performed (1-2 senten
 ces).\n\n* Suggest at least one way each method/experiment could be improv
 ed (1-2 sentences).\n\nHere is a hypothetical example of how this should l
 ook:\n\n1. Neanderthal Genetics: One anthropologist compared Neanderthal D
 NA to that of modern humans and determined that some humans today have Nea
 nderthal ancestry. Five Neanderthal samples were compared to a large group
  of over 1000 living people. If this study had included a larger sample si
 ze of Neanderthals\, it could have strengthened the connection to modern h
 umans.\n\n------------\n  Submission\n------------\n\nSubmit your abstra
 ct as one of the following by Friday at 11:59 p.m.: \n\n* .docx\n\n* .doc
 \n\n \n\nImage Credits\n-------------\n\nMike Searcy\, Eagle's Watch 2\, 
 Mike Searcy\, Used with Permission.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser onl
 y)\n\n 
